  "bug": {
    "bug_id": "Lang-12",
    "project": "Lang",
    "summary": "RandomStringUtils.random(count, 0, 0, false, false, universe, random) always throws java.lang.ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException",
    "description": "In commons-lang 2.6 line 250 :\n\nch = chars[random.nextInt(gap) + start];\n\nThis line of code takes a random int to fetch a char in the \nchars\narray regardless of its size.\n\n(Besides \nstart\nis useless here)\n\nFixed version would be :\n\n//ch = chars[random.nextInt(gap)%chars.length];\n\nWhen user pass 0 as \nend\nor when the array is not null but empty this line ends up with an exception"
  },
